<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Altranstädt (1706)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1706</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Altranstädt of 24 September 1706, made near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> participation in the war after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII of Sweden</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>. Augustus the Strong renounced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a> in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski">Stanisław Leszczyński</a>, broke his alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and handed over the Livonian Johann Patkul, whom the Swedes executed. The Swedish army wintered in Saxony at the country's expense.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-altranstadt-1706.jpg" alt="Treaty of Altranstädt (1706)" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altranstadt_Mittagessen_1706.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
